      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Religious conservatives fundamentally oppose medical aid in dying because they view life as a sacred gift from God that humans do not have the authority to end. They argue that participating in euthanasia violates the sanctity of life and undermines the inherent value of every human being, regardless of suffering. Conversely, religious liberals often support it, arguing that compassion and the alleviation of unbearable suffering align with core tenets of mercy and love. They contend that allowing individuals autonomy over their own bodies and deaths is a moral imperative rooted in divine care.",
