      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that's a decent start, but i need more depth for a grad paper. the conservative side feels a bit simplified—like it's just \"don't do it because God said so.\" can you expand on the actual philosophical or theological frameworks they use to justify that? for example, how do they handle the problem of extreme, unmitigated suffering? and on the liberal side, can you go deeper into the specific theological concepts they use to support bodily autonomy? i want to see the actual logical structures they're building.",
